{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-12T05:13:34.929Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"72bc6070cdf8e143b3ffadf4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1703"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1703: pm context spends a third of its default output on a fixed omission receipt whose restore hints are all --section <name>"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1703 (filed 2026-11-11). Every default pm context call ends with an omission_receipt listing the ten sections the default projection leaves out, one row each, and every restore hint is the plain --section name form. Measured on a fresh two-item tracker: default TOON 1,449 B with a 505 B receipt (35 percent), --json 2,733 B with 684 B. The receipt is identical on every default call, so it is a fixed cost at the start of every session and the largest block on small trackers. Proposal: when the omitted set is exactly the documented default, emit one compact line of omitted section names plus a single restore template; keep the per-row table only for rows whose restore command is not derivable from the name (a budget cut, a truncated list, a requested section that could not be served); apply the same rule to other omission receipts whose restore hints are derivable from the row name."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","context","gh:1703","output","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","valu